        {
          "kicker": "Red Roses result",
          "heading": "England women end 41-match unbeaten run as Canada win 24-21 in Toronto",
          "body": "England women were beaten 24-21 by Canada in Toronto on Friday, a first defeat since 2022 that ends a 41-match unbeaten run. Canada had drawn 26-26 with England at Sandy Park in September, and their semi-final dismantling of New Zealand at last year's World Cup showed how far they have closed the gap on the world champions. Sale hooker Amy Cokayne, who has 95 caps, faced the press this week: \"You can't dwell on it.\" The teams meet three times this autumn in the WXV Global Series."
        },
