      "edition": "Wednesday 21 October",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Selection call",
          "heading": "Steve Tandy leaves door open for Taulupe Faletau's 2027 World Cup bid",
          "body": "Taulupe Faletau, 35, has been left out of Steve Tandy's 39-man squad for the Nations Championship, despite returning from injury for Cardiff against Northampton on Sunday. Tandy has not ruled the Wales great out of the 2027 World Cup in Australia, saying he can \"see the drive in him\" and that Faletau must first put consistent rugby together. The 109-cap number eight has not played under Tandy and has played at three World Cups, missing 2019 with a collarbone injury."
        },
        {
          "kicker": "Around the world",
