    "461": {
      "date": "2026-10-21",
      "edition": "Wednesday 21 October",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Northern tour",
          "heading": "Harry Wilson, Fraser McReight back Wallabies' UK tour after Bledisloe loss",
          "body": "Skipper Harry Wilson and flanker Fraser McReight are confident the Wallabies can bounce back on tour, with the opener at Twickenham against England followed by Scotland and Wales. Wilson said he \"probably never felt under so much pressure\" as in the last two games against the All Blacks, the 43-21 Sydney loss and the 50-19 Eden Park defeat before it. McReight, who has fond memories of Twickenham's 2024 win over England, says the All Blacks are \"world-class for a reason.\""
        },
        {
          "kicker": "Around the world",
          "heading": "England women's unbeaten run ends with 24-21 defeat to Canada",
