    "465": {
      "date": "2026-10-21",
      "edition": "Wednesday 21 October",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Team gesture",
          "heading": "All Blacks went out early to honour Nathan Charles ahead of Sydney Test",
          "body": "The All Blacks went out early for Saturday's second Bledisloe Cup Test at Accor Stadium so they could go over to former Wallabies hooker Nathan Charles, who has revealed his Motor Neurone Disease diagnosis. The whole team went to him on the field, and captain Codie Taylor later presented him with a framed All Blacks jersey signed by the squad. Ex-All Blacks scrum-half Justin Marshall called the gesture \"incredible\" on a podcast."
